  "body": "Found in M5's review of PR #1615 (pullrequestreview-5900983707): a **whole-model 2D Adaptive with default settings** on the repo's `Milling-test.step` generates a toolpath that **gouges the part 10 mm deep at about (-1.44, -29.94)**.\n\n- **Before #1615:** nothing judged a whole-model 2D Adaptive on the op. With an aligned stock the program sim blocked the post; with a turned stock it would have posted (#1603).\n- **With #1615's keep law:** it is refused on the op on both stocks, and the op law and the program sim agree.\n\nSo the generator itself produces a gouging path with default controls; the new law only catches it. Rated P3 by the table (wrong behaviour a user hits: a legal default operation is refused, the workaround is to change the region or strategy). If #1615 does not merge, or the keep law stands down (no stock set up), it is a P1.\n\n**Done means:** a whole-model 2D Adaptive with defaults on Milling-test.step generates a path that stays outside the part (zero gouges on the op and in the sim). The cause in the generator is found and fixed, pinned through `operation::generate`, and mutation-checked.\n\nRelated: #1603, #1615, #1554.\n",
